  abstract = {Let \$X = (X\_1, \textbackslash cdots, X\_n)\$ where the \$X\_i: p \textbackslash times 1\$ are independent random vectors, and let \$A: n \textbackslash times n\$ be positive semi-definite symmetric. This paper establishes necessary and sufficient conditions that the random matrix \$XAX'\$ be positive definite w.p.1. The results are applied to cases where \$A\$ has a particular form or \$X\_1, \textbackslash cdots, X\_n\$ are i.i.d. In particular, it is shown that in the i.i.d. case, the sample covariance matrix \$\textbackslash sigma(X\_i - \textbackslash bar\textbraceleft X\textbraceright )(X\_i - \textbackslash bar\textbraceleft X\textbraceright )'\$ is positive definite w.p. 1 \$\textbackslash operatorname\textbraceleft iff\textbraceright{} P\textbackslash lbrack X\_1 \textbackslash in F\textbackslash rbrack = 0\$ for every proper flat \$F \textbackslash subset R\textasciicircum p\$.},
